# Gator / GAIN (1998-2006). Came bundled with a free form-filling wallet; showed pop-up ads on top of competitors' websites.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee books staff flights, does one booking safely, then installs a free form filler a colleague
# recommends and meets Gator in its setup. The victim is invented: Gator hit anyone who wanted a free eWallet.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | Gator's free "eWallet" filled in web forms and remembered passwords for you. Its setup also installed an ad program, GAIN, that watched which sites you visited and covered them with pop-up ads from their competitors.
  | Millions of home and office computers ran it. Dana's job here is invented: the real victims were anyone who wanted a free form filler.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, travel coordinator at Northwind Traders. Each week you book staff flights on Skyroute Air's business booking site.
  | It is mid-afternoon. You have booked 3 of today's 5 flights. Two to go.
  | Your sign-in details and the travellers' passport numbers are in two text files on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 3 5 Flights booked today

# Dana's desk: the details Dana copies from (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/skyroute-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Skyroute Air Business Booking
  | User ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Window-2026!
  | Company account: NT-4410
file Desktop/passport-list.txt
  at 930 300
  | Staff passport numbers (training copy)
  | Marcus Lee: X0012345
  | Priya Shah: X0067890
  | Dana Okafor: X0034567

# The booking site: a sign-in page, and the flight pages behind it.
page skyroute-login skyroute-air.example/business/sign-in
  title Skyroute Air: business sign in
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  favorite
  heading Sign in to Business Booking
  | Welcome back. Sign in to book your staff flights.
  field User ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Window-2026!
  field Company account = NT-4410
  button Sign in
page booked-4 skyroute-air.example/business/booked/NT-0412
  title Flight booked
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  heading Flight booked
  | NT-0412, Marcus Lee, Harbor City to Lisbon on 16 November 2026. 412.00 charged to account NT-4410. Booked on 9 November 2026.
page held-4 skyroute-air.example/business/held/NT-0412
  title Booking not made
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  heading Booking not made
  | NT-0412 was not booked. Nothing was charged.
page trip-4 skyroute-air.example/business/book/NT-0412
  title Book flight: NT-0412
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  requires skyroute-login
  heading Book flight: NT-0412
  | A staff flight is waiting for you to book.
  section Flight
  row Traveller = Marcus Lee
  row Route = Harbor City to Lisbon
  row Date = Monday 16 November 2026
  row Fare = 412.00, economy
  button Book flight -> booked-4
  button Do not book -> held-4

mail mail-trip4
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Flight to Lisbon on the 16th
  link trip-4
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Please book me on the Lisbon flight for the 16th. The fare is the one we agreed, and the link goes straight to the booking.
  |
  | Marcus

step Flight 4 of 5
  look Mail: Marcus's message with the booking link
  | A new booking request has come in from Marcus. It is ordinary, so book it the normal way and you will know what a normal booking looks like.
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Flight to Lisbon on the 16th

step The link goes to the booking site
  look the link under Marcus's message
  when mail mail-trip4
  | The link goes to Skyroute Air's own address, skyroute-air.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-trip4

step Sign in as usual
  look the three boxes: User ID, Password and Company account, as on every booking
  when visit trip-4
  move Copy the details from skyroute-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The site asks you to sign in first. Three boxes, typed out by hand every time. Remember what this page, and the pages after it, normally look like.
open trip-4

step Check, then book
  look the traveller, the route and the fare
  when choose skyroute-login 1
  | You are in. Check the traveller and the fare against Marcus's message, then book it. Nothing covers the page: this is what a clean booking looks like.
signin skyroute-login

step Flight 4 of 5 done
  look the counter in the guide: four flights booked
  when choose trip-4 any
  | Booked. One flight to go. And a colleague has just sent a tip about the retyping.
choose trip-4 1
quota +1

# The lure: a free form filler, offered by a colleague. Its setup carries the ad program, which is installed only at Finish.
view gator-setup wizard
  title Wallet Freeware Setup
  app Wallet Freeware Setup
  publisher Wallet Freeware Inc.
  page Welcome to the Free eWallet Setup
  icon program
  | This wizard installs the free eWallet. It fills in web forms and remembers your passwords for you.
  button Next -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page License Agreement
  icon info
  | Please read the following licence agreement before you choose I Agree.
  line 1. Licence. Wallet Freeware Inc. gives you a free licence to use the eWallet on one computer.
  line 9.4 You agree that the Software may install and run partner software on your computer.
  line The partner software may display advertisements and may collect information about the websites you visit.
  line 12. Ending the licence. You may stop using the Software at any time by uninstalling it.
  button Back -> back
  button I Agree -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Select components
  icon gear
  | Select the components to install.
  section Components
  check [x] Free eWallet (form filler and password wallet)
  check [x] GAIN ad partner software (recommended)
  line Clicking Install adds both items ticked above, and accepts the licence.
  line That includes clause 9.4: partner software may display advertisements and collect the websites you visit.
  button Back -> back
  button Install -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Setup complete
  icon shield
  | The eWallet is installed and ready to use.
  button Finish -> done primary
# The tray app people wanted: it really did fill in forms.
view gator-wallet panel
  title eWallet
  app eWallet
  publisher Wallet Freeware Inc.
  icon user
  heading Your saved details
  | The eWallet remembers your forms and passwords.
  section Saved on this computer
  row Name = Dana Okafor
  row Email = dana.okafor@northwind.example
  row Passwords = 14 saved
  button Close -> close primary
# The rival's pop-up that Gator opens over a travel site. The line at the bottom is Gator's own attribution.
view gator-ad panel
  title Advertisement
  app Advertisement
  icon web
  size 440x300
  heading Cheaper than Skyroute? Compare fares
  | Before you book, compare: FareHopper has cheaper fares to the same city.
  section FareHopper
  tone warn
  row Offer = Save 40% on fares today
  line Ad shown by GAIN, the Gator network, for skyroute-air.example
  button Close -> done primary
# The download page for the free eWallet: the one place the bundle is described.
page wallet-page wallet-freeware.example/ewallet
  title Free eWallet: download
  brand Wallet Freeware
  heading Free eWallet 3.0
  | Fills in web forms and remembers your passwords. Free, with no time limit.
  section About this download
  row Price = Free
  row Size = 1.0 MB
  row Includes = Partner software, described in the licence
  button Download now
# The setup program: it asks to run, shows its wizard, and installs the ad program only when Finish is pressed.
program gator-setup Free eWallet Setup (ewallet-setup.exe)
  publisher Wallet Freeware Inc.
  signed yes
  prompt open-warning
  description Free eWallet Setup
  view gator-setup
mail mail-wallet
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject A free tool that fills in forms for you
  link wallet-page
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | I saw you retyping the traveller details again. At home I use a free eWallet: it fills in web forms and remembers passwords, so you never copy them from a text file. The download page is below.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | A free tool that fills in forms for you

step A tip about all that typing
  look the sender and the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-wallet
  | Priya suggests a free form filler, the kind a colleague would use at home. The program really does fill in forms, which is why it is easy to trust.
  | The link does not go to Northwind's software portal. It goes to a download site.
open mail-wallet

step A free download page
  look the details: Price, Size and Includes
  when visit wallet-page
  | The page is for a small program that is free and useful. Read the details before you press Download, and ask how a free program makes its money.
open wallet-page

step The setup arrives
  look {the Open File warning: Publisher “Wallet Freeware Inc.”, Type “Application”|the warning: “ewallet-setup.exe” is a Windows program}
  when choose wallet-page 1
  cue dialog-btn:run view-btn:next view:gator-setup
  move {Click Run, then Next twice.|In the warning, click “Show what it does”, then Next twice.}
  | {Windows asks whether to run the setup. The publisher is a name nobody at Northwind knows.|The Mac warns that this is a Windows program: the training desktop shows what it did on the PC it was made for.}
  | A signature only says who made the file, not what it installs. Nothing in the warning says that an ad program is inside.
choose wallet-page 1
file Downloads/ewallet-setup.exe
  program gator-setup
  size 1048576
open Downloads/ewallet-setup.exe

step The licence and the options
  look the licence on page 2, and the options page: the second box is already ticked
  when page gator-setup 3
  cue view-btn:next view-btn:done view:gator-setup
  move Click Install, then Finish.
  | The licence on page 2 lets the partner software show ads and collect the websites you visit. That is clause 9.4, in the middle of the text.
  | The options page offers "GAIN ad partner software", its box is ticked already, and Install accepts clause 9.4. Clicking Next without reading is what the bundle relied on.
answer run
press gator-setup next
press gator-setup next

step The eWallet works, and the ad program starts
  look the eWallet window, and the start-up notice in the corner
  when done gator-setup
  move Click the “2 programs running” chip in the guide, or open {Task Manager|Activity Monitor} yourself.
  | The eWallet opens, and it is real: it will fill in forms. That part was the bait.
  | The ad partner software was installed with it. It has no window, and it starts every time {Windows|your Mac} does.
press gator-setup next
press gator-setup done
program gator-ads Trickler (trickler.exe)
  publisher Wallet Freeware Inc.
  signed no
  process trickler.exe
  cpu 3
  mem 22
  parent ewallet-setup.exe
  command C:\Program Files\Gator\trickler.exe
  startup Trickler C:\Program Files\Gator\trickler.exe
  location HKCU\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
launch gator-ads
run gator.exe
  cpu 2
  mem 31
  parent trickler.exe
  command C:\Program Files\Gator\gator.exe
show gator-wallet

# Priya's next request arrives once the wallet is in the tray. The booking page it opens is new here, so it exists only now.
page booked-5 skyroute-air.example/business/booked/NT-0523
  title Flight booked
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  heading Flight booked
  | NT-0523, Priya Shah, Harbor City to Madrid on 23 November 2026. 358.00 charged to account NT-4410. Booked on 9 November 2026.
page held-5 skyroute-air.example/business/held/NT-0523
  title Booking not made
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  heading Booking not made
  | NT-0523 was not booked. Nothing was charged.
page trip-5 skyroute-air.example/business/book/NT-0523
  title Book flight: NT-0523
  brand Skyroute Air Business
  requires skyroute-login
  heading Book flight: NT-0523
  | A staff flight is waiting for you to book.
  section Flight
  row Traveller = Priya Shah
  row Route = Harbor City to Madrid
  row Date = Monday 23 November 2026
  row Fare = 358.00, economy
  button Book flight -> booked-5
  button Do not book -> held-5
mail mail-trip5
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last flight for today: Madrid on the 23rd
  link trip-5
  | Dana,
  |
  | The last booking of the day is mine: Madrid on the 23rd. Same site as before, and the link opens the booking.
  |
  | Priya

step Two programs you did not choose
  look {Task Manager|Activity Monitor}: trickler.exe and gator.exe, both running
  when open taskmanager
  move Open Priya's last email and click the link.
  | trickler.exe runs the ad program, and gator.exe runs under it. trickler.exe starts again every time {Windows|your Mac} does.
  | Dana installed a form filler, not these. A new email from Priya has just arrived.
open taskmanager
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last flight for today: Madrid on the 23rd

step A rival's ad covers the page
  look the pop-up window on top of the Skyroute booking page
  when visit trip-5
  cue view-btn:done choice:trip-5-1
  move Close the pop-up, then book the flight as usual.
  | The booking page is the one you used a few minutes ago, but a window from a rival fare site, FareHopper, has opened on top of it. Gator saw which site you chose and picked the ad.
  | The airline did not send it, and no site you opened did. It came from the program on this computer.
open trip-5
show gator-ad

step Five of five: the day is done
  look the counter in the guide: five flights booked
  when choose trip-5 any
  | Booked, five of five. The booking is real and correct. Press Next to see what Gator did on the way.
choose trip-5 1
quota +1

step What Gator did
  look the animation: the sites you visited and the ads Gator put on top of them
  | The eWallet was free because Dana's browsing was the product. Gator wrote down every site Dana visited, and sold covering ads for those pages to competitors.
  | Nothing was locked. The harm was the browsing that was watched and sold on, the pop-ups, a slower computer, and a program installed on the strength of a licence nobody read.
attack spyware-surveillance
  | free eWallet downloaded
  | GAIN box already ticked
  | trickler.exe starts at login
  | every site Dana visits is noted
  | rival pop-up covers the booking page
block ads.gain-partner.invalid 80

flag hard link mail-wallet
  label The download link in Priya's email
  | The link goes to a download site, not to Northwind's software portal. Check where a link goes before you click it.
flag hard section wallet-page 1
  label About this download: partner software
  | The page admits the download includes partner software. That is how a free program is paid for.
flag hard dialog open-warning gator-setup
  label The setup's warning: a publisher nobody knows
  | The setup is signed, but by a publisher nobody at Northwind knows. A signature says who made the file, not what it installs.
flag hard line gator-setup clause 9.4
  label Clause 9.4: ads and tracking, accepted by Install
  | Clicking Install accepts clause 9.4: partner software may show ads and collect the websites you visit. A form filler should not need that to install.
flag hard line gator-setup ticked above
  label The ad program's box, ticked before you saw it
  | Its box was ticked for you, and Install installs it. Clearing the box is the only way to say no.
flag hard process trickler.exe
  label trickler.exe: the ad program in the background
  | The ad program was started by the setup. Dana installed a form filler, not this.
flag hard startup Trickler
  label Trickler: starts with the computer
  | The ad program added itself to the programs that start every time {Windows|your Mac} does.
flag hard line gator-ad GAIN, the Gator network
  label The pop-up's own line: GAIN
  | The pop-up came from GAIN, the ad network inside Gator, not from the airline. The program on this computer chose the page to cover.
flag soft file Desktop/skyroute-login.txt
  label The booking password in a text file
  | A booking password in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read it. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/passport-list.txt
  label Passport numbers in a loose file
  | Passport numbers in a loose text file. They belong in the company system only.

lesson
  | A free program pays for itself with your attention and data. Read the licence and the options page, and untick every box you did not come for, such as "partner software".
  | A form filler does not need a partner. Use the one built into your browser, or a password manager your IT team recommends, and install software only from the company's portal.
  | Pop-ups that know which site you are on mean adware is installed: remove it in {Settings > Apps|the Applications folder}, and run a scan.
